    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on levin-2022-grn-learning-21: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.73";
    dc:description "The differential degradation result is directly reproducible. The proposed selective cause is historical and is not discriminated from model complexity or curation effects.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Repeat matched edge-addition and deletion trajectories and compare memory degradation between biological and random models. This resolves robustness, while attributing it to evolutionary pressure requires alternative nulls or comparative selection evidence.";
